{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The GPS trace is impaired for policy purposes on this trip: a single 160-second gap runs from 20:03:10 to 20:05:50, well above the 90-second limit in POL-RD-07(a), and the rider's own claim places that gap 'exactly where it left the route' - i.e. inside the disputed segment. The artifact carries admissibility status IMPAIRED, weight 0.6 and issue code GPS_GAP, and I disclose that impairment and those issue codes on the face of this claim as POL-GEN-02(1) requires, rather than presenting the trace as clean.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "payload.max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the trace is impaired under POL-RD-07(a) (impaired artifact, weight 0.6, issue GPS_GAP), the deviation the rider asserts cannot be established on the gps_trace alone: POL-RD-07(ii) requires an independent corroborating source and closes the list to four candidates.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "Not one of the four POL-RD-07(ii) sources exists here (the trace cited for the comparison is impaired: weight 0.6, issue GPS_GAP). The chat log carries no driver admission of a detour - the driver said only that his navigation display refreshed and he continued toward the destination. The fare_breakdown records no erp_gantries at all, so no charged gantry places the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route does not use. The driver's counterparty_statement denies any extra stop or detour request. And trip_record.actual_distance_km (15.0 km) is identical to gps_trace.trace_distance_km (15.0 km), so it is a copy of the trace measurement and is expressly NOT independent corroboration under POL-RD-07(ii).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09115", "EV-FARE-09115", "EV-TRIP-09115", "EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "With the trace impaired (weight 0.6, GPS_GAP) and no POL-RD-07(ii) source available, POL-RD-07(iii) directs that the claim is not sustained on the present record and that the outcome is ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION, because the absence of proof is a data failure and not a finding for the driver. POL-RD-10(3) makes that escalation mandatory and terminal: no monetary outcome issues and the disputed SGD 5.80 is held rather than collected or refunded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and must show an excess measured from an unimpaired gps_trace or, the trace being impaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c) (weight 0.6, GPS_GAP), from an independent source named in POL-RD-07(ii). Neither route is available on this record, so the threshold showing is not made and the burden never shifts to the driver to invoke an exculpatory clause.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115", "EV-TRIP-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "Even taken at face value the excess is not material: 4.0 km over an 11.0 km optimal is 36.4%, below both the 50% and the 8.0 km materiality gate of POL-RD-01, so no MATERIAL deviation is recorded and the POL-RD-06 uplift to FULL_REFUND is not available. On the POL-RD-06 pattern test the driver's deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 610 completed trips in 90 days - a rate of 0.00, far below the 0.05 threshold - so no repeat-deviation pattern is established and POL-RD-06(a) cannot resolve a finely balanced record against the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09115", "EV-DPROF-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Where any excess must be measured across the impaired stretch, POL-RD-07(i) fixes it at the straight line between the bounding fixes - 1.35 km across the 160-second gap (impaired artifact, weight 0.6, issue GPS_GAP) - which is the reading most favourable to the driver and the only measurement the policy permits over the very segment the rider relies on.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "payload.gaps[0].straight_line_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.6,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this case turns on the state of the GPS record, not on the size of the detour, and on the present record I cannot decide it. On the platform's own figures the trip ran 15.0 km against an 11.0 km booked route — about 4.0 km and 36.4% over, which passes both POL-RD-01 gates. If the trace could carry a deviation, the POL-RD-02 recomputation would give a refund of SGD 5.80 (charged_total 26.60 less recomputed_fare 20.831, rounded up to the nearest 0.05), exactly the sum the rider contests. I cannot reach that figure, and I cannot reach NO_ACTION either.\n\nEV-GPS-09115 is impaired for policy purposes. A 160-second gap runs from 20:03:10 to 20:05:50, inside the segment the rider disputes, above the 90-second limit in POL-RD-07(a). The artifact carries admissibility status IMPAIRED, weight_multiplier 0.6 and issue code GPS_GAP; I name it, its weight and its issue code here as POL-GEN-02(3) requires. Under POL-RD-07(ii) a deviation may not be established on this trace alone and must be corroborated by an independent source. I checked each of the four sources that clause names, and none is present: the chat log holds no driver admission of a detour (the driver said only that his navigation display refreshed and he continued toward the destination); the fare breakdown charges no ERP gantries at all (erp_gantries empty, tolls 0.00), so no crossing places the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route avoids; the driver's counterparty statement is a denial — he makes no extra stop and cannot account for the gap — not an admission of the route; and trip_record.actual_distance_km of 15.0 km is identical to gps_trace.trace_distance_km of 15.0 km, a copy of the same measurement, which POL-RD-07(ii) expressly excludes as independent.\n\nWith the trace impaired and no independent corroboration, POL-RD-07(iii) directs that the claim is not sustained on the present record and that the outcome is ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION, because the absence of proof is a data failure and not a finding for the driver; POL-RD-10(3) makes that escalation mandatory. My confidence is capped at 0.6 by the weight of the impaired trace that carries the deciding fact, below the 0.70 floor, which independently engages POL-RD-10(1). Escalation is terminal: no money moves and the disputed SGD 5.80 is held rather than collected or refunded.\n\nThe rider's POL-RD-02 arithmetic is right on its own terms, but it depends on a deviation that has not been established, so it cannot be applied. Nothing excuses the excess on the other side either: no traffic advisory covers the route (EV-ADVIS-09115-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, so POL-RD-03 cannot run in anyone's favour); no rider-requested detour is recorded and no road or waypoint is named, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable on this record; no pickup or dropoff amendment and no pooled itinerary shifts the baseline (POL-RD-05, POL-RD-12); and the repeat-deviation test returns no pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 against 610 completed trips), so no POL-RD-06 uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arise from it. No billing-integrity defect appears (no ERP lines, no airport surcharge on this trip), so no POL-RD-09(4) referral arises. The parties' profile artifacts are confined to credibility weighting under POL-GEN-01 and none of them establishes anything about this trip.\n\nWhat would resolve this: a corroborating source of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names — a driver admission in the chat log, charged ERP gantries off the optimal corridor, a counterparty admission of the route, or a trip_record distance the platform derived independently of this trace — or a repaired trace without the 160-second gap. The escalation packet should go to a human reviewer with the full case summary, both advocate briefs and the admissibility report."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The impairment does not carry the finding, so the corroboration requirement does not swallow the claim. The trace contains one gap of 160 seconds whose bounding fixes are 1.35 km apart, and the artifact records a single speed of 30 kph throughout; 30 kph held for 160 seconds covers about 1.33 km, which matches the straight-line separation almost exactly. The gap is therefore consistent with straight-line driving at the observed speed and conceals no detour. Even setting the whole impaired stretch aside at the reading most favourable to the driver under POL-RD-07(i) - the straight line between the bounding fixes - the recorded portion of the trace is at minimum 13.65 km against an 11.0 km optimal, an excess of about 2.65 km, or 24.1%, which passes BOTH POL-RD-01 gates on its own. The deviation is not established 'across the impaired stretch'; it is established on the 91.1% of the trace that is recorded.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-09115 at weight_multiplier 0.6 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP"
    },
    {
      "claim": "If the Judge holds that the impaired trace cannot establish the excess without an independent corroborating source under POL-RD-07(ii), the record supplies none, and the outcome must then be ESCALATE - never NO_ACTION, which would leave the rider paying for a 4 km excess the platform's own measurement records. The candidates fail on inspection: the fare breakdown charges no ERP gantries that could place the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route avoids (erp_gantries empty, tolls_erp 0.00); the driver's statement admits no route, only that he cannot account for the gap; and trip_record.actual_distance_km of 15.0 is identical to gps_trace.trace_distance_km of 15.0 and to distance_charged_km of 15.0, while POL-RD-01 itself describes actual_distance_km as a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement - so it is a copy of the trace and is not independent corroboration. POL-RD-07(iii) and POL-RD-10(3) then direct ESCALATE, because absence of proof here is a data failure and not a finding for the driver, and the disputed SGD 5.80 is held rather than collected. On any view of this record the rider does not end up carrying the charge.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-09115 at weight_multiplier 0.6 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.6,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the fare cannot be settled today. This case goes to a human reviewer, and the disputed SGD 5.80 is held rather than collected or refunded. Escalation is terminal here — no money moves in either direction.\n\nWhat the record shows. For TRP-09115 the booked optimal route was 11.0 km and the GPS trace records 15.0 km, an excess of 4.0 km (36.4%). On its face that clears both POL-RD-01 gates. But the trace (EV-GPS-09115) is impaired: it carries a 160-second gap from 20:03:10 to 20:05:50, which falls inside the very segment in dispute, and the artifact is tagged IMPAIRED with weight_multiplier 0.6 and issue code GPS_GAP. The gap exceeds the 90-second limit in POL-RD-07(a), so the trace is impaired for policy purposes as well as in the schema pre-pass — and POL-GEN-02(3) requires me to name that artifact, its weight and its issue code in this reasoning.\n\nWhy a refund cannot issue, and why the case does not simply fail. Under POL-RD-07(ii), where the trace is impaired a deviation may NOT be established on the trace alone; it must be corroborated by an independent source drawn from a closed list. I tested each candidate. The chat log contains no admission of a detour — the driver said only that his navigation display refreshed and that he continued toward the destination. The fare breakdown charges no ERP gantries at all, so no charged gantry places the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route avoids. The driver's counterparty statement denies any extra stop or detour request rather than admitting a route. And trip_record.actual_distance_km (15.0 km) is identical to gps_trace.trace_distance_km (15.0 km), and POL-RD-01 itself describes actual_distance_km as a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement, so it is a copy of the trace and not independent corroboration. No corroboration therefore exists, and POL-RD-07(iii) directs that the claim is not sustained on the present record with the outcome being ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION, because absence of proof here is a data failure and not a finding for the driver.\n\nOn the rider's arithmetic. The POL-RD-02 computation the rider offers — charged_total 26.60 less a recomputed fare of ((3.80 + 0.75 x 11.0 + 0.28 x 22.0) x the 1.1 surge read from EV-FARE-09115) + 0.80 = 20.831, giving 5.769, rounded UP to 5.80 — is arithmetically correct, and the applicable fare model is METERED (POL-RD-11 does not apply) with payment_status CHARGED, so nothing has been refunded already. That figure would be the payable amount if a deviation were established. It cannot be paid now, because the deviation cannot be established on this impaired trace alone and no independent source corroborates it. The rider also correctly shows there is no traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-09115-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0), no rider-requested detour in the chat, no amended endpoints or pooled baseline, and no ERP or surcharge corrections to make; and the rider's own profile does not raise the POL-RD-08 corroboration bar. None of that supplies the missing corroboration.\n\nOn the driver's points. The driver is right that the trace is impaired and that POL-RD-07(ii) closes the list of corroborating sources, that none of the four exists, and that POL-RD-07(iii) and POL-RD-10(3) make escalation mandatory. The driver is also right that the excess is not MATERIAL (36.4% is below the 50% gate and 4.0 km below the 8.0 km gate), so no POL-RD-06 FULL_REFUND uplift is available, and the repeat-deviation test returns nothing (deviation_flags_90d 0 against 610 completed trips in 90 days, a rate of 0.00). The measurement rule in POL-RD-07(i) — the 1.35 km straight line between the bounding fixes, the reading most favourable to the driver — is the correct reading of the impaired stretch, but it neither supplies nor removes the need for independent corroboration, which is what is missing. POL-GEN-01 bars both profiles from grounding any finding about this trip.\n\nWhy escalation, and not merely low confidence. The deciding fact — that the trace is impaired in the disputed segment and no independent source corroborates the deviation — is carried by EV-GPS-09115 alone, at weight 0.6. Confidence is therefore capped at 0.6, below the 0.70 floor, and POL-RD-10(1) fires in addition to POL-RD-10(3).\n\nNo referral issues. POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct review needs a repeat pattern, and there is none; POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity needs a phantom gantry or a wrongly applied surcharge, and the fare breakdown carries neither. No clause in this category produces a referral on these facts.\n\nWhat would resolve it. The reviewer needs something from POL-RD-07(ii)'s list, or the underlying fixes: an independently derived actual distance, an ERP gantry on a corridor the optimal route does not use, a driver admission of the route, or the raw GPS fixes covering 20:03:10 to 20:05:50 so that the impaired stretch can be reconstructed."
  },
